Subject: [PATCH] soft: preserve computed targets when statistics are invalid

An invalid statistics frame may still contain an older captured exposure
and gain. Keep the latest prepared automatic targets in that case, instead
of scheduling the older captured values again. Metadata continues to
describe the actual captured controls and their source.

---
diff --git a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/algorithms/agc.cpp
@@ -243,9 +243,9 @@
 
 	/* Targets belong to this request; metadata above belongs to the captured SOF. */
 	bool sourcesMatch = frameContext.sensor.source == frameContext.agc.source();
-	if (!frameContext.agc.autoExposure || !sourcesMatch)
+	if (!frameContext.agc.autoExposure || !sourcesMatch || !stats->valid)
 		frameContext.sensor.exposure = frameContext.agc.exposure;
-	if (!frameContext.agc.autoGain || !sourcesMatch)
+	if (!frameContext.agc.autoGain || !sourcesMatch || !stats->valid)
 		frameContext.sensor.gain = frameContext.agc.gain;
 	if (!stats->valid || !sourcesMatch ||
 	    (!frameContext.agc.autoExposure && !frameContext.agc.autoGain))
